\begin_inset Formula $i=1,\ldots,n-1$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{i}\succ x_{i+1}$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{1}=x_{n}$
\end_inset

.
 Prove that if 
\begin_inset Formula $X$
\end_inset

 is finite, then 
\begin_inset Formula $\succeq$
\end_inset

 is 
\begin_inset Formula $\succ\mbox{- acyclic}$
\end_inset

 if and only if for each 
\begin_inset Formula $B\subseteq X$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $B\neq\emptyset$
\end_inset

, 
\begin_inset Formula $C^{\succ}(B)\neq\emptyset$
\end_inset

.
