\end_inset

 s.t.
 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{1}\succ\ldots\succ x_{n}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\implies x_{1}=x_{n}$
\end_inset

 since 
\begin_inset Formula $\succeq$
\end_inset

 is 
\begin_inset Formula $\succ\mbox{- cyclic}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Now, 
\begin_inset Formula $x_{1}\succ\ldots\succ x_{n-1}\succ x_{n}=x_{1}\succ\ldots\succ x_{n-1}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
So, 
\begin_inset Formula $\succ$
\end_inset

 is not transitive
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Formula $\implies\succeq$
\end_inset

 is not transitive
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Thus, 
\begin_inset Formula $ $
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $\succeq$
\end_inset

 is complete and 
\begin_inset Formula $\succ\mbox{- cyclic}\implies\succeq\mbox{is not transitive}$
\end_inset

,
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
which is equivalent to 
\begin_inset Formula $\succeq\mbox{is complete and transitive}\implies\succeq\mbox{is}\succ\mbox{- acyclic}$
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
\emph on
End Claim
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset VSpace medskip
\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Since 
\begin_inset Formula $B$
\end_inset

 is finite, then 
\begin_inset Formula $\succeq$
\end_inset

 is a 
\begin_inset Formula $\succ\mbox{- acyclic}\iff C^{\succ}(B)\neq\emptyset$
\end_inset

 by problem 4
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Also, since 
\begin_inset Formula $\succeq$
\end_inset

 is a rational preference relation, then 
\begin_inset Formula $C^{\succeq}(B)=C^{\succ}(B)$
\end_inset

 by problem 3
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Therefore, 
\begin_inset Formula $ $
\end_inset


\begin_inset Formula $C^{\succeq}(B)\ne\emptyset$
\end_inset


\end_layout

